{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:9398629 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:9398629 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"9398629","source":"MED","pmid":"9398629","doi":"10.1006/bbrc.1997.7724","title":"Nuclear accumulation of G-actin in isolated rat hepatocytes by adenine nucleotides.","authorString":"Meijerman I, Blom WM, de Bont HJ, Mulder GJ, Nagelkerke JF.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Meijerman I","firstName":"I","lastName":"Meijerman","initials":"I","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Division of Toxicology, Leiden-Amsterdam Center for Drug Research, Leiden University, The Netherlands. meyerman@lacdr.leidenuniv.nl"}]}},{"fullName":"Blom WM","firstName":"W M","lastName":"Blom","initials":"WM","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-6853-0900"}},{"fullName":"de Bont HJ","firstName":"H J","lastName":"de Bont","initials":"HJ"},{"fullName":"Mulder GJ","firstName":"G J","lastName":"Mulder","initials":"GJ"},{"fullName":"Nagelkerke JF","firstName":"J F","lastName":"Nagelkerke","initials":"JF"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-6853-0900"}]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"3","volume":"240","journalIssueId":1094240,"dateOfPublication":"1997 Nov","monthOfPublication":11,"yearOfPublication":1997,"printPublicationDate":"1997-11-01","journal":{"title":"Biochemical and biophysical research communications","medlineAbbreviation":"Biochem Biophys Res Commun","essn":"1090-2104","issn":"0006-291X","isoabbreviation":"Biochem Biophys Res Commun","nlmid":"0372516"}},"pubYear":"1997","pageInfo":"697-700","abstractText":"Extracellular ATP induces bleb formation in isolated rat hepatocytes. We examined the effect of extracellular ATP on the actin cytoskeleton of these hepatocytes. Exposure to 100 microM ATP caused pronounced nuclear accumulation of G-actin. ADP, AMP, adenosine, and dibutyryl-cAMP induced the same effect. Adenosine deaminase could inhibit both ATP- and adenosine-induced nuclear accumulation. The P2-receptor agonists, UTP and 2' & 3'-O-(4-benzoylbenzoyl)-adenosine 5'-triphosphate, did not induce this redistribution of G-actin. Phalloidin, which prevents depolymerisation of F-actin filaments to G-actin monomers, inhibited adenosine-induced nuclear accumulation of G-actin. These observations suggest that nuclear accumulation of G-actin is mediated by adenosine receptors.","affiliation":"Division of Toxicology, Leiden-Amsterdam Center for Drug Research, Leiden University, The Netherlands. meyerman@lacdr.leidenuniv.nl","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Liver","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"CY","qualifierName":"cytology","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"DE","qualifierName":"drug effects","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism","majorTopic_YN":"Y"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cells, Cultured"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cell Nucleus","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism","majorTopic_YN":"Y"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cytoskeleton","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Rats"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Phalloidine","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"PD","qualifierName":"pharmacology","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Actins","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism","majorTopic_YN":"Y"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Adenosine Deaminase","meshQual